/-!
# Z31 dark-corner audit — BIP341 ext-flags/annex framing in sigmsg +
# SIGHASH_DEFAULT-as-ALL semantics

2026-10-16. Python3 probes:
`z31_crosscheck.py`,
`z31_crosscheck2.py` — all checks PASS, official corpus
`spec/vectors/bips/bip-0341_wallet-test-vectors.json` keyPathSpending[0]
re-derived 7/7 + Core v26.0 interpreter.cpp read directly).

Ground truth (Core, VERIFIED from v26.0 source this audit):
* C1: `SignatureHashSchnorr` :1508-1512 (`spend_type = (ext_flag << 1) +
  have_annex`, `ss << spend_type`), :1547-1556 (input slice, then
  `[sha_annex] iff annex`, then `[sha_single_output] iff SINGLE`);
  annex detection :1907-1915 (`stack.size() >= 2 && !stack.back().empty()
  && stack.back()[0] == ANNEX_TAG` → pop, `m_annex_hash =
  (HashWriter{} << annex).GetSHA256()` — `<<` on a valtype writes the
  CompactSize length, so sha_annex = SHA256(CSize(len) ‖ annex incl 0x50)).
* C2: :1509 `output_type = (hash_type == SIGHASH_DEFAULT) ? SIGHASH_ALL :
  (hash_type & SIGHASH_OUTPUT_MASK)` — DEFAULT (0x00) is ALL semantics,
  NOT a distinct mode; :1510 input mask `ht & 0x80` (0x00 → non-ACP, same
  as ALL); :1512 `ss << hash_type` (the 0x00 byte still enters the
  message); :1686-1689 64-byte sig ⇒ implicit DEFAULT, 65-byte sig with
  trailing 0x00 ⇒ SCHNORR_SIG_HASHTYPE error.

TWO assertion lanes (Z29/Y16 discipline; kernel whnf stops at sha256, so
computed cases use the `#eval` + `#guard_msgs` lane — build FAILS on any
divergence; cheap structural facts use the `decide` lane). Axiom-free.

NOTE (2026-10-16): this file is DELIBERATELY self-contained — it does NOT
import `BitcoinProofs.Bip.B13.B13SigMsg` (X03's file was transiently
broken on disk during the audit build; see F-Z31-004). The env
below (`txV`/`outsV`) is byte-for-byte the official keyPathSpending[0]
`rawUnsignedTx`/`utxosSpent` decode, generated by
generated by a small script and cross-checked against
X03's B13SigMsg `tx9`/`outs9` literals (identical) and against the
python mirror (7/7 official sighashes re-derived, `z31_crosscheck2.py`).
-/

namespace Bitcoin.Proofs.Audit.Z31

open Bitcoin.Data
open Bitcoin.Crypto.Taproot (sigMsgTaproot sighashTaproot shaAnnex spendType
  extFlagOf htOutputAll htAcp htNone htSingle hashtypeValid TapSighashEnv)
open Bitcoin.Crypto.Taproot.Program (isAnnex classifySpend)
open Bitcoin.Crypto.Seam (ScriptExecutionData SigVersion)
open Bitcoin.Crypto.Seam.Entry (SIGHASH_DEFAULT schnorrHashtype)

set_option maxRecDepth 10000
set_option maxHeartbeats 2000000

-- hex helper (Z29/Z01 pattern)
private def hexDigitVal (c : Char) : Option Nat :=
  let n := c.toNat
  if 48 ≤ n ∧ n ≤ 57 then some (n - 48)
  else if 97 ≤ n ∧ n ≤ 102 then some (n - 87)
  else none

private def fromHex (s : String) : ByteArray :=
  go (s.toList.filter (fun c => c != '\n' && c != ' ')) ByteArray.empty
where
  go : List Char → ByteArray → ByteArray
    | [], acc => acc
    | [_], acc => acc
    | a :: b :: rest, acc =>
        match hexDigitVal a, hexDigitVal b with
        | some ha, some hb => go rest (acc.push ((ha * 16 + hb).toUInt8))
        | _, _ => go rest acc

